<BaseLayout
  title="Grokking or Glitching? How Floating-Point Precision Drives Training Loss Spikes | AI/ML Deep Dives"
  description="Slingshot loss spikes during long neural network training are not an optimizer quirk — they are a floating-point artifact. This post explains the Numerical Feature Inflation feedback loop and why casting only the loss computation to float64 makes the spikes vanish entirely."
