  <h1>Grokking or Glitching? How Floating-Point Precision Drives Slingshot Loss Spikes</h1>
  <p class="lead">Periodic loss spikes during long neural-network training — the "Slingshot Mechanism" — have puzzled researchers for years, blamed on optimizer dynamics or grokking. This paper proves they are floating-point artifacts: casting only the loss computation to float64 makes every spike vanish. The culprit is <em>Numerical Feature Inflation</em>, a precision-induced feedback loop that exponentially inflates the global means of classifier weights and features until the loss explodes.</p>
